# 🧮 Principali Misure DAX - Insurance Churn Analytics

Qui di seguito sono elencate alcune delle misure DAX chiave sviluppate per il modello semantico in Power BI, volte a calcolare il rischio e l'impatto economico.

## 1. Churn Rate (%)
Calcola la percentuale di clienti persi rispetto al totale del portafoglio polizze.
```dax
Churn Rate % = 
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(Policies[ClientID]), Policies[Status] = "Churned"),
    DISTINCTCOUNT(Policies[ClientID]),
    0
)

## 2. Revenue at Risk = 
CALCULATE(
    SUM(Policies[PremiumAmount]),
    Policies[RiskScore] > 75,
    Policies[Status] = "Active"
)

## 3. Average Premium
Average Premium = AVERAGE(gold_insurance_renewals[Premium_Amount])

## 4. Avg Price Increase %
Avg Price Increase % = AVERAGE(gold_insurance_renewals[Price_Increase_Pct])

## 5. Avg_Risk_Score
Avg_Risk_Score = AVERAGE(gold_insurance_renewals[Risk_Score_Index])
## 6. Total Policies 
Total Policies = COUNT('gold_insurance_renewals'[Policy_ID])
